rom $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -7 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-35792/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "595fd527-e8fd-5360-87f1-acbeab511566"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35792"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81825/selection/ac18eecde072949ed97b77d9024019cb292d2c90e29dabdaef9f83d6d2669152" :answer/id #uuid "63749493-2e3b-5cd8-9a84-f48b14beb613" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a=1,$ $b=-5,$ and $c=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81825/selection/ab4303b7ab43d8e6e016d16bc1f15768d557dcef0a3aec76525dde4b525588f0" :answer/id #uuid "48ba82e7-861b-50dc-a6a2-c74700beab56" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a=3,$ $b=0,$ and $c=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81825/selection/3dea2e4dbf0231e147deb8fef5410081f0619699868eee185b56bee82e7afd26" :answer/id #uuid "362505ae-3f7b-5ec2-9688-6f11f5c6bbb5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a=3,$ $b=4,$ and $c=0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81825/selection/fa6f6fb8e94d326358ca10348d905012644da2a25c35ce15849402260c1f64e9" :answer/id #uuid "aad49c0b-3b5e-53dc-971d-624ed8ef78be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a=-1,$ $b=0,$ and $c=0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81825/selection/3983a2edbc75fab80f37c1011d1173f49bb37e3817bf5b89bd63e8c15444a9b7" :answer/id #uuid "eaa80bed-64be-5ebb-b39d-08253db29def" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a=-1,$ $b=4,$ and $c=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81825/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7953d339-0fdf-52f1-8dba-62f7b1861982" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81825/selection/3983a2edbc75fab80f37c1011d1173f49bb37e3817bf5b89bd63e8c15444a9b7" :answer-field/choices ["q-81825/selection/ac18eecde072949ed97b77d9024019cb292d2c90e29dabdaef9f83d6d2669152" "q-81825/selection/ab4303b7ab43d8e6e016d16bc1f15768d557dcef0a3aec76525dde4b525588f0" "q-81825/selection/3dea2e4dbf0231e147deb8fef5410081f0619699868eee185b56bee82e7afd26" "q-81825/selection/fa6f6fb8e94d326358ca10348d905012644da2a25c35ce15849402260c1f64e9" "q-81825/selection/3983a2edbc75fab80f37c1011d1173f49bb37e3817bf5b89bd63e8c15444a9b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81825" :question/id #uuid "cebf33a6-1e88-5dcd-a020-6375d9d328e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-81825" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}}$ be bases of ${R}^{3}.$ \nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} & =3{b}_{3}-{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}, \\\\ {c}_{2} & =4{b}_{2}-5{b}_{1}, \\\\ {c}_{3} & =2{b}_{1}+3{b}_{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}a & -5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & b & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & c\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the vectors in $C$ relative to the basis $B$ are\n\n$$\n[{c}_{1}]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,[{c}_{2}]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[{c}_{3}]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $C$ relative to the basis $B.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=-1,$ $b=4,$ and $c=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81825/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "595fd527-e8fd-5360-87f1-acbeab511566"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81825"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} 