0c5abfb7605735629ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-81394"] :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}}$ be bases of ${R}^{3}.$ \nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}-{c}_{3}, \\\\ {b}_{2} & =5{c}_{3}+2{c}_{2}, \\\\ {b}_{3} & ={c}_{2}-{c}_{1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ a & b & 1 \\\\ -1 & c & 0\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C$ are\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{3}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=2,$ $b=2,$ and $c=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81394/selection/ma-v1/bbeae7bd8a4ddd8fd029a1f51b72461e67d60d69bca64360136dd946747e7c6d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-36366"] :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $S$ be the standard basis of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to S}$ from $B$ to $S$ if \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall  that the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ consists of the vectors ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2},$ given by\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors of $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-36401/selection/556d75c35d1ec35f745b9ad5e7199461c229acd3075b8e96913b9f76afb80d8d" :answer/id #uuid "b89a8d5d-2282-57e6-b817-861f04ebfaf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36401/selection/248b6f5e4117d38807d9efcf0a76bd1134c2183ef0bc8f1a9e65d081d881893e" :answer/id #uuid "dfc74b44-b8cb-5743-ba22-a0231e1d9641" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36401/selection/f4e6ae5d529ead799010eaca383278089139ebde1f4c21dbfdbc6040dc440ae3" :answer/id #uuid "560867dc-8a4f-5e51-8b96-8a2d62246b84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36401/selection/de33a13086de313e6c970518ecee39b5c0944591ca76e6cdc622f21b9cfadce6" :answer/id #uuid "7bc0b5b5-1d53-5747-ac95-dfcd76757a24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36401/selection/54c29537cf15cac8d4b3212cbf0c5de82a24966ed1e76a6354e66d9526eb47b2" :answer/id #uuid "78b458bf-c099-5ec8-94b2-2a75e69824a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36401/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "023f