s given by\n${P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$  ." :question/worked-solution "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C} & ={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 9}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-113413/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "23b6a85e-e1de-590c-84d2-379052b1b9f3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113413"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113520/selection/6d56dc8e818b4436d856d4b2c82372d8f26d3fe310be4d21efe5bd3ffd751043" :answer/id #uuid "0ca23ca6-bb6d-561a-8da2-a041611dea09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113520/selection/1e8dcc807e07637a8414f88f8b8e8088f461a95babde5c2215b646fafcc275bb" :answer/id #uuid "af26bf47-93e7-5bc5-9456-0448647b39be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113520/selection/68b8f2fba2100753db29bf28874e73be08d50b6e031f6d7b0f688067baacfd39" :answer/id #uuid "e097af62-101a-5dae-8610-6353119b1ff0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113520/selection/7defd6b7cec1bfeb8ee244612eb2dfa6d6a76e5e734333ec402637e10e5d5c93" :answer/id #uuid "fcb8f6e1-5439-5cc2-a2ed-687be3b8e063" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113520/selection/f8d32fb2524e048f4405f51bffcdbde7bdbc955c3cfe3aa254b09bb4b9c87ba5" :answer/id #uuid "f183fa21-594a-57a0-b5b5-7f8b6105a02a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113520/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f7bcaad0-35c3-59ba-bf45-21872573d9de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-113520/selection/7defd6b7cec1bfeb8ee244612eb2dfa6d6a76e5e734333ec402637e10e5d5c93" :answer-field/choices ["q-113520/selection/6d56dc8e818b4436d856d4b2c82372d8f26d3fe310be4d21efe5bd3ffd751043" "q-113520/selection/1e8dcc807e07637a8414f88f8b8e8088f461a95babde5c2215b646fafcc275bb" "q-113520/selection/68b8f2fba2100753db29bf28874e73be08d50b6e031f6d7b0f688067baacfd39" "q-113520/selection/7defd6b7cec1bfeb8ee244612eb2dfa6d6a76e5e734333ec402637e10e5d5c93" "q-113520/selection/f8d32fb2524e048f4405f51bffcdbde7bdbc955c3cfe3aa254b09bb4b9c87ba5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-113520" :question/id #uuid "3c47c537-5fe9-53d3-b29a-26acc7d1e093" :question/math-academy-id "q-113520" :question/problem "Let $B={[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}$ and $C={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}$ be bases of ${R}^{2}.$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-113520/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f989cbaf-2d99-5267-8864-48a48db2d535"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113520"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-36398/selection/be2ad730beea511f509f97931f88b1dcdeaeeb96d486240fca99577987ce0d8b" :answer/id #uuid "87bebe9d-bb37-5824-94ce-fe561aa6bfeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36398/selection/1edc19ebb085c18910c314065e565bd91232a0c09dca920aadfc0e497f4db885" :answer/id #uuid "ef65e3ec-0962-5c12-a4ba-e04d5e6e0ee9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36398/selection/1bc6dce93c7bd9088e45f56ce2d713838122ab44ffaaa8f249bcbb13adc64a38" :answer/id #uuid "fca9a934-c8d2-5fd2-8f37-9ba92b1a2200" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36398/selection/8a40d8639ec904e07271b89790b46a7add6bd8b02dbbd9b50ac28bb7c22ed5f4" :answer/id #uuid "258b39bb-3