dering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 3 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-36398/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f989cbaf-2d99-5267-8864-48a48db2d535"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36398"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113510/selection/6590d9e67202cdcaade7f13144670430e389b4f113d04cb5ddaa36efb3e5d73a" :answer/id #uuid "21293c50-75f5-590e-b4d1-65b7bf3084f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113510/selection/e5f8f0fe01fcb90c2adc82baf1b9d892154934cf5d4947bcab00d3000cd184c4" :answer/id #uuid "23b65d6f-72ee-5e43-86f7-60521a53ab1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113510/selection/d9f12de10b113086330142af50d768c960333be9ff09292dfa67915624d8b8f1" :answer/id #uuid "3767a592-f2a6-5e7a-ad9e-ad21d6e80d68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113510/selection/c138a59d1ea94c5aee1bde5d322c25fab91ce7acb8471d3b2f38e7ecc8191824" :answer/id #uuid "8e46a25b-451b-5