ing the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 9 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-113510/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f989cbaf-2d99-5267-8864-48a48db2d535"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113510"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113513/selection/6da0045d166ec7953d0529f076854b65585698f0a621325f1f558dbcff5396aa" :answer/id #uuid "325ac13f-4566-5a7e-bf93-25f023d35026" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113513/selection/9d35998ae9fdbd8a2a9c7698f5c8d39d753aca244a7fb29e910ab759009ba5f4" :answer/id #uuid "dc90ddc8-546b-5db8-afc2-7e42f793937e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113513/selection/537547cf63145b6817738fc0b2e369b88e87cf25b75408975b1a7549f3fbba37" :answer/id #uuid "2d63c9e0-2100-5e1c-ae84-cda3ae6601b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 